+# Veterinarian Search Stays Out; Filtering the Directory by a Shown Attribute Is In
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners as the only searchable entity. Like most Non-Goals rows, it was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey. Its provenance stayed open.
+
+On 2026-09-11 the owner requested narrowing the veterinarian directory to one specialty. Read whole, NG-9 excludes that request. The owner decided the row in the same intake.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-9 whole.** Decline the specialty filter as a form of veterinarian search.
+2. **Lift NG-9 for veterinarians.** Admit veterinarian search of every kind, free text included.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen). Keep free-text veterinarian search out, and admit filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows.
+
+## Decision
+
+The owner's decision, quoted from the intake record:
+
+> Non-goal NG-9 is narrowed: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in. Record the narrowing the way the project records non-goal changes.
+
+The line falls between filtering by what the directory already shows and searching by free text. The intake record states no reason beyond the decision, and this ADR adds none.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Free-text veterinarian search is a decided exclusion, no longer a survey artifact.
+- Filtering the veterinarian directory by an attribute it already shows is in scope. The specialty filter, `REQ-VET-003`, is the first such filter.
+- A filter on any other shown attribute still arrives as its own request. This decision admits it without requesting it.
+- Pet and visit search stay in NG-9 with open provenance. This decision does not touch them.
+- The same intake reinstated the machine-readable veterinarian list as a supported surface, `REQ-VET-004`. That is a requirement decision recorded in the PRD, not part of this non-goal change.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row and the updated preamble.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the first filter the narrowing admits.
